For Loop Example Questions

Print all numbers from 1 to 10 using a for loop.

Calculate the sum of numbers from 1 to 100 using a for loop.

Print each element in the list fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"].

Print all even numbers between 2 and 20 using a for loop.

Iterate through a string and print each character.

While Loop Example Questions

Print numbers from 1 to 10 using a while loop.

Calculate the factorial of a given number using a while loop.

Prompt for user input repeatedly until the user enters the string "quit".

Print the Fibonacci sequence up to a certain number using a while loop.

Use a while loop to find the first number greater than 100 that is divisible by 17.

Nested and Advanced Loop Questions

Use nested for loops to print the elements of a matrix (list of lists).

For numbers from 1 to 100, print "Fizz" for multiples of 3, "Buzz" for multiples of 5, and "FizzBuzz" for multiples of both 3 and 5.

Write a program that keeps asking the user to enter integers, and stops when a negative number is entered (then print the average of the non-negative numbers).

Given a list of lists, print all items using nested loops.
